ral Station's misery, oiled and humming."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Squeeze', 'text': "The dame vanished. Of course she did. Frank Delaney found her scarf in the office, red as a warning, and underneath it a note: 'Forgive me. They have my brother.' So that was the price. Everyone has one.\n\nRuby's club was next — a fire in the kitchen, a message in the smoke. Frank Delaney found her unharmed and furious, and that fury was worth ten guns. 'End this,' she said. Frank Delaney intended to.\n\nMr. Big squeezed back. First the office: tossed, the safe cracked, a ledger of names's copy gone — but Frank Delaney keeps the originals where no one looks. Then Doc Ellison: a warning delivered with fists in an alley off Grand Central Station."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Confrontation', 'text': "Frank Delaney walked into Mr. Big's office at noon, when Grand Central Station was bright and honest-looking, which made the lies inside seem darker. a ledger of names went on the desk. The photographs went on the desk. The truth went on the desk.\n\nThe dame got her brother back and Frank Delaney got the rest of the fee, which was more than the insulting original. She cried. Frank Delaney didn't buy the tears but didn't charge for the shoulder, either.\n\n'You're finished,' Frank Delaney said. Mr. Big smiled the smile of someone who has bought judges. 'Am I?' Then Doc Ellison opened the door with the district attorney, and Ruby, and the dame's brother, alive, and the smile died."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Last Call', 'text': "The dame left town on the morning train, brother in tow, free and clean. She left Frank Delaney a note: 'You were the only honest thing in it.' Frank Delaney kept the note. Detectives keep everything.\n\nLou poured a double on the house. Ruby sang the song she only sings when she means it. Doc Ellison's ribs were taped, but Doc Ellison drank anyway, doctor's orders being for other people.\n\na ledger of names went into the office safe, next to the other honest things. Someday, Frank Delaney knew, someone would walk in with something like it, and it would start again. It always starts again."}]}

